        "documentation-contract",
        "timeout-test-stability",
        "verification"
      ],
      "summary": "Model self-review (not independent or human): no blocking findings. The todo surface exposes one view-only refresh controller while every todo execution still reruns the workflow resolver, preserving fresh authority selection and preventing standalone synchronization. Successful SWE operations update focus then refresh cached completions/status/widget; presentation failures are bounded and cannot turn a durable lifecycle mutation into an apparent failure. Registration remains singular. Integration coverage reproduces the original stale completion defect, verifies status/widget refresh, authority switching, fail-closed malformed authority, and presentation-failure semantics. Documentation now matches fail-closed missing/unreadable focus behavior. The resistant-child timeout fixture uses a lightweight shell process so the restored 200ms timeout remains meaningful under load while preserving SIGTERM-ignore/process-group-kill coverage. Typecheck, 27 focused tests, 234 full tests, repository checks, command inventory, and release verification pass on the final bounded source set.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "pi-model-self-review",
        "sessionId": "01a0d003-d43e-74cb-9306-ff7d91c3d67e"
      }
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D-1",
      "text": "Preserve fresh backend resolution for execution and add only an explicit presentation refresh path after successful SWE mutations.",
      "basis": "The defect is stale cached guidance, not authority selection or mutation routing."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-2",
      "text": "Missing or unreadable focused authority remains fail-closed and documentation must say so.",
      "basis": "Fail-closed behavior prevents accidental writes to standalone authority when workflow focus is stale or corrupted."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-3",
      "text": "Keep the HUD wall-clock assertion load-tolerant but restore the short configured timeout input.",
      "basis": "This retains behavioral coverage without relying on strict scheduler timing under full-suite concurrency."
    }
  ],
  "risks": [
    {
      "id": "R-1",
      "text": "Refresh wiring could cache or reuse a backend and reintroduce stale-authority mutation risk.",
      "mitigation": "Refresh view-only state through a callback that reruns the existing resolver; leave execution resolution unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-2",
      "text": "SWE mutation refresh could duplicate widgets or registrations.",
      "mitigation": "Reuse the existing todo surface instance and expose one bounded refresh callback rather than registering new handlers."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-3",
      "text": "The 200ms HUD timeout case could remain flaky under load.",
      "mitigation": "Retain the short configured timeout but use a generous wall-clock assertion and confirm in the full suite."
    }
  ]
}
